DualContrast is more substantive than the lowest anchors (DisFormer, Causal VAE) because it tackles real scientific data and provides compelling downstream qualitative results. However, it is below the medium anchor (GMG, 5.50) because its own quantitative evidence undermines its core claims. A paper whose Table 1 shows worse separation than baselines on 2/3 datasets, whose ablation improves separation when removing a core loss, and whose flagship claim lacks standard quantitative validation, cannot be considered above the acceptance threshold. The RELION results are promising but insufficient to override the metric contradictions.

