SecureGS is stronger than the low-scoring watermarking papers (3.75–4.00) by virtue of its focused technical contributions and direct comparisons to prior art. However, it sits below the medium-scoring diffusion-watermarking paper (5.33) because the confounded experimental comparisons and qualitative-only security analysis are more severe weaknesses. The paper’s core idea is reasonable, but the headline empirical claims cannot be cleanly attributed to the proposed steganographic mechanisms.

