Even if the causal graph terminology is reframed as hierarchical concept-graph propagation, the intervention training procedure—randomly clamping prior concept logits during training to simulate evidence injection—functions as an effective form of partial-evidence regularization and data augmentation. This technique could generalize beyond the current framework to other structured prediction problems where partial human feedback is available at test time.

